[The definition fails]: A guess made on evidence that turns out right is not always a good guess.
    <+ [The coin guess was informed]: The coin guess was made on the evidence of past tosses.
        {about: {case: B, informed: yes}}
    <+ [The coin guess was right]: The coin guess turned out right.
        {about: {case: B, right: yes}}
    <+ [The coin guess was not good]: The coin guess was not a good guess, since it was right by luck.
        {about: {case: B, good: no}}
    <- [The definition]: A good guess is one made on evidence that turns out right. #reported
